WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.499
(chill rock)

00:00:02.499 --> 00:00:04.504
- Kinda like a skater has a skateboard,

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.559
or a BMXer has a bike,

00:00:06.559 --> 00:00:08.189
I just saw the wheelchair
as something fun,

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:10.939
so why not take it into the park?

00:00:15.057 --> 00:00:16.943
I'm Aaron "Wheelz" Fotheringham

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:18.987
and I ride WCMX.

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:21.801
WCMX stands for Wheelchair Motocross.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.319
It's, you know, taking your chair

00:00:23.319 --> 00:00:25.484
into the skate park and hitting ramps.

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:28.340
Kind of the same thing as
BMX, but with a wheelchair.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.096
I first started going to the skate parks

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.288
when I was eight years old.

00:00:31.288 --> 00:00:33.823
And I've been doing it for 16 years now.

00:00:33.823 --> 00:00:36.776
The wheelchair's definitely
just an extension of my body,

00:00:36.776 --> 00:00:39.973
because skaters aren't
always on their skateboard,

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.653
and bikers aren't always on their bike,

00:00:41.653 --> 00:00:42.875
but I'm always on my chair.

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:45.004
So that gives me like an unfair advantage

00:00:45.004 --> 00:00:46.794
to just practice everywhere I go.

00:00:46.794 --> 00:00:48.302
I feel like I'm lucky that I always

00:00:48.302 --> 00:00:49.912
have my wheelchair with me, 'cause I can

00:00:49.912 --> 00:00:52.079
just jump whenever I want.

00:00:54.224 --> 00:00:55.800
I was born with spina bifida.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.332
I've had 21 surgeries throughout my life.

00:00:58.332 --> 00:01:00.779
And I spent a lot of
time in the hospitals.

00:01:00.779 --> 00:01:04.350
And yeah, it would be easy to
just be bummed out on that,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.693
but I was, for me, I
just found the positive.

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:10.443
The wheelchair's just
always been fun, and,

00:01:10.443 --> 00:01:12.937
it's wheels, stuck to your butt.

00:01:12.937 --> 00:01:15.112
How's that not a great time?

00:01:15.112 --> 00:01:16.858
(wonderous music)

00:01:16.858 --> 00:01:19.431
In 2008, I got the Guinness World Record

00:01:19.431 --> 00:01:21.973
for the first back flip on a wheelchair.

00:01:21.973 --> 00:01:23.692
And that was at a local competition

00:01:23.692 --> 00:01:25.568
here in Vegas called Am-Jam.

00:01:25.568 --> 00:01:27.340
That was a pretty cool day.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:31.074
One of my favorite tricks
is just a simple hand plant.

00:01:31.074 --> 00:01:33.280
Because I always loved watching skaters

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.725
do it when I was growing up, and, you know,

00:01:35.725 --> 00:01:38.345
watching the pros do it,
it just was something

00:01:38.345 --> 00:01:39.845
I wanted to learn.

00:01:43.752 --> 00:01:45.923
I'm very blessed to be
able to do what I love

00:01:45.923 --> 00:01:49.079
and what I'm passionate
about for a living.

00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:50.611
A lot of the time, the wheelchair comes

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:52.820
with the stereotype of "you can't do this"

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.389
or whatever, because
it's a medical device.

00:01:56.389 --> 00:02:00.556
I just always think the
wheelchair's a great opportunity.

00:02:03.465 --> 00:02:06.048
(simple tones)

